<h1>Preferences - Datums - Form Tolerances</h1>
<hr align="left" width="100.526%" size="5" class="whs3">
<p>Form Tolerances settings define the tolerances during tactile datum capture.</p>
<p><img src="Images/preferences_datums_form_tolerances.gif" width="593px" height="367px" border="0" class="img_whs4" alt=""></p>
<p class="sub-head">Out of tolerance notification group</p>
<p>These options enable the tolerance check for an entity during capture. If it is enabled then when a point for this entity is captured the entity is fitted with the previous points. If the distance between the last point and the fitted entity is higher than the given tolerance then a warning sound is played and information message is displayed in yellow. For example, if datum point is captured with tolerance 0.01mm and the distance between the third point and the point fitted by the first two points is 0.203mm (which is higher than the given tolerance of 0.01mm), KUBE will play warning sound and will display the following message:</p>
<p class="Bullet"><img src="Images/out_of_tolerance_point.gif" width="802px" height="150px" border="0" class="img_whs5" alt=""></p>
<p>The information in the message is as follows:</p>
<ul class="whs6">
<li style="text-align:justify; margin-left:-20px;" class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet" style="margin-left:38px;">Capture point... - the entity that is currently captured (point, line, plane, etc.)</p>
</li>
<li style="text-align:justify; margin-left:-20px;" class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet" style="margin-left:38px; font-weight:normal;"><span class="Button" style="font-weight:normal;">Captured points: 3 - the last captured point for the entity that is out-of-tolerance.</span></p>
</li>
<li style="text-align:justify; margin-left:-20px;" class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet" style="margin-left:38px;">Tolerance: 0.203 - distance in mm <span class="Button" style="font-weight:normal;">between the last point and the entity fitted with the previous points.</span></p>
</li>
</ul>
<p>User may continue to capture accepting the point or may delete it by holding the '<span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>B</b></span>' button.</p>
<p>These options are disabled by default and the default tolerances are 0.01mm. The options are applied to the following entities:</p>
<p class="parameterstitle">Point</p>
<p class="parameterdescription">Distance between the last point and the fitted point is checked.</p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span class="Button">Line</span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><span class="Button" style="font-weight:normal;">Distance between the last point and the fitted line is checked.</span></p>
<p class="parameterstitle">Plane</p>
<p class="parameterdescription">Distance <span class="Button" style="font-weight:normal;">between the last point and the fitted plane is checked.</span></p>
<p class="parameterstitle">Sphere</p>
<p class="parameterdescription">B<span class="Button" style="font-weight:normal;">etween the last point and the surface of the fitted sphere is checked.</span></p>
<p class="parameterstitle">Cylinder</p>
<p class="parameterdescription">B<span class="Button" style="font-weight:normal;">etween the last point and the surface of the fitted cylinder is checked.</span></p>
<p class="parameterstitle">Circle</p>
<p class="parameterdescription">B<span class="Button" style="font-weight:normal;">etween the last point and the circumference of the fitted circle is checked.</span></p>
<p class="parameterstitle">Cone</p>
<p class="parameterdescription">B<span class="Button" style="font-weight:normal;">etween the last point and the surface of the fitted cone is checked.</span></p>
